l` must be flagged. License is","+  AGPL-3.0: assess whether Apple's App Store terms raise a GPL/AGPL","+  compatibility concern (the copyright holder can distribute their own","+  code, but third-party AGPL/GPL dependencies may matter). Present this as a","+  risk with sources, not as legal advice.","+"," ## Task breakdown"," ","-<!-- TASK-1: description","-     files: list of files likely affected","-     depends: none","-     risk: low / medium / high — reason","+TASK-1: Inventory the current build/release/distribution setup relevant to store publishing (APK vs AAB, signing flow, versioning, CI, F-Droid signing, manifest permissions, existing fastlane metadata) and write it up as a \"current state\" section.","+  files (read-only): android/app/build.gradle, android/variables.gradle, android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml, android/app/src/main/java/app/solyto/*.java, capacitor.config.json, package.json, scripts/build-fdroid.sh, scripts/release.sh, .github/workflows/release.yml, fdroid/app.solyto.yml, fastlane/metadata/android/**; output in docs/reports/play-store-and-app-store.md (new)","+  depends: none","+  risk: low. It is a read-only inventory; reading release.sh is fine but it must never be executed."," ","-TASK-2: ...","--->","+TASK-2: Verify app-level compliance prerequisites that both stores share: in-app account deletion (backend + `../app`), privacy policy URL, and what user data leaves the device (for Data safety / privacy labels). Mark each item present, missing, or unknown, and say which repo owns the fix.","+  files (read-only): frontend/src/lib/config/apiRoutes.ts, frontend/src/lib/config/platform.ts, frontend/src/routes/profile/+page.svelte, frontend/src/routes/settings/+page.svelte, frontend/src/routes/auth/register/+page.svelte, frontend/src/service-worker.ts; output in report","+  depends: none","+  risk: medium. The account-deletion gap is probably a hard blocker for both stores and lives outside this repo, so state it carefully and verify it