w rules; web push not working in WKWebView/Android WebView; keeping `build-fdroid.sh` offline/Node 20 and F-Droid unaffected; vendored-frontend workflow for any JS changes; whether any `fdroid/app.solyto.yml` change is needed (flag it).","+  files (read-only): scripts/build-fdroid.sh, scripts/vendor.sh, fdroid/app.solyto.yml, LICENSE, frontend/src/lib/config/platform.ts; output in report","+  depends: TASK-3, TASK-4","+  risk: medium. Licensing and review-guideline interpretation are judgement calls, so they must be framed as risks for the maintainer to decide.","+","+TASK-6: Assemble the final report `docs/reports/play-store-and-app-store.md`. It should contain: a summary (blockers first), current state (TASK-1), shared prerequisites (TASK-2), a Google Play step list (TASK-3), an App Store step list (TASK-4), risks/constraints (TASK-5), a phased plan (e.g. fix blockers → Play closed testing → Play production → iOS project → TestFlight → App Store), costs and accounts needed, a work split by repo (this repo / `../app` / backend), open questions for the maintainer, and dated sources. Follow the style of `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`.","+  files: docs/reports/play-store-and-app-store.md (new)","+  depends: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5","+  risk: low. It is documentation only, with no build or runtime impact.","+","+## Unclear / for the maintainer","+","+- The brief has no \"Why\" or \"Out of scope\". The analyst assumes the report","+  covers *steps only* and implements none of them (no AAB build, no iOS","+  scaffold, no CI changes).","+- Whether the developer account(s) are personal or organization accounts","+  (this affects Play's testing requirement and Apple's D-U-N-S requirement) is","+  unknown. The report should cover both paths.","+- Whether a Mac is available for iOS builds is unknown. The report should","+  cover local Xcode as well as hosted macOS CI.","+- Whether the app stays free with no in-app purchases is assumed (the brief",