{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg7zujwd2jtUyh1vdHwEa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the task list to `docs/jobs/jail_play-store-and-app-store-strategy/tasks.md`. It plans one report, `docs/reports/play-store-and-app-store.md`. Nothing in the app gets changed: no new build format, no iOS project, no CI or signing changes.\n\nI couldn't confirm we're on the `report/jail_play-store-and-app-store-strategy` branch, because I have no shell in this session. Please check that before the developer starts.\n\n**Tasks**\n1. **Current setup (low risk):** how the app is built, signed, versioned and released today, including the F-Droid build and the existing store text and screenshots.\n2. **Requirements both stores share (medium risk):** account deletion, a privacy-policy URL, and what user data leaves the device.\n3. **Google Play steps (medium risk):**\n   - developer account and identity check\n   - the testing period Google requires from new accounts\n   - switching from APK to the bundle format Play requires\n   - how Google's signing fits with the existing key and F-Droid\n   - data safety form, content rating, store listing, release tracks\n4. **Apple App Store steps (high risk):**\n   - developer program and the Mac/Xcode requirement\n   - creating an iOS project\n   - iOS versions of the Android-only features: share target, pull-to-refresh, edge-to-edge\n   - setup for passkeys to work on iOS\n   - privacy labels, TestFlight and App Review\n\n   This is the riskiest part: no iOS project exists yet, and Apple sometimes rejects apps that mainly wrap a website.\n5. **Other risks (medium risk):** whether the AGPL-3.0 licence conflicts with App Store terms, the custom server URL and the user-supplied OpenAI key under review rules, web push not working inside the app, and keeping the F-Droid build working.\n6. **Final report (low risk):** blockers first, then a phased plan, costs, which repo owns each piece of work, open questions and dated sources.\n\n**Likely blocker:** people can register inside the app, but I found no way to delete an account, either in the API route list or on the profile page. Both stores require account deletion when sign-up happens in the app. The fix would be in the backend and the main web app repo (`../app`), not here. I've asked the developer to double-check this before the report states it.\n\n**Questions for you** (also listed in tasks.md):\n- Are your developer accounts personal or organisation accounts? This changes Play's testing rules and whether Apple needs a D-U-N-S number.\n- Do you have a Mac for iOS builds, or would you use hosted macOS CI?\n- I've assumed the app stays free with no in-app purchases. Is that right?\n- Is the report filename OK? I picked it myself."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4348,"cache_read_input_tokens":32720,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4348},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"debe97b1-540a-4869-be59-f7c5d9cf8b55","uuid":"f3923f3c-b029-49da-a021-80d9e41e8f27","timestamp":"2026-10-17T14:53:00.364Z","request_id":"req_011Cg7zujfVr1mim2QHRRDjt"}
