{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GaHdze67MFnB6UqEeRsaPq","type":"tool_result","content":" Play Console APIs ↗️\n the Android Developer's Blog\n Read the latest\n Explore the authors →\n Explore categories\n Product News\n Community\n How-tos\n Case Studies\n Events & Programs\n Documentation\n Android Developers\n Essentials\n Android developer verification\n Stay organized with collections\n Save and categorize content based on your preferences.\n Android developer verification\n By making Android safer, we're protecting an environment for developers and users to confidently create and connect. This extra layer of security helps deter bad actors and makes it harder for them to repeatedly spread harm.\nEffective September 30, 2026\n Protections begin for users installing apps from \nparticipating stores\n in select regions on \ncertified Android devices\n. We'll continue rolling out user protections globally in 2027.\n Choose your verification path\n Wherever you choose to distribute your apps, Google supports you in your developer journey. Review the guides to\n understand your account options and potential fees.\nAndroid Developer Console\n Distribute exclusively outside Google Play\n For developers distributing apps exclusively outside of Google Play.\nGuide\nConsole\nGoogle Play Console\n Distribute on and outside Google Play\n Google Play automatically registers 99% of apps. Use Play Console to manually register remaining apps or those distributed outside Google Play.\nGuide\nConsole\n Timeline\nWe're announcing these changes early and incorporating developer feedback to help keep the Android ecosystem safe and sustainable.\nMilestone\nDetails\nAugust 2026\nDeveloper APIs, limited distribution accounts, and power user advanced flow launch.\nSeptember 30, 2026\nProtections begin for all users who install apps from participating stores in Brazil, Indonesia, Singapore, and Thailand on certified devices running Android 7+.\n2027 and beyond\nVerification capability will be expanded globally for all apps on certified\n Android devices in 2027.\n Get support\n Guides\n Explore technical documentation and video guides.\n FAQ\n Find quick answers about registration fees, requirements, and signing keys.\n Help Center\n Visit the \nAndroid Developer Console Help Center\n or \nPlay Console Help Center\n for account troubleshooting and support.\nAdvanced Flow:\nExplore\n how we'll serve power users who want the ability to download unverified apps.\nLatest News\nGuide\n Register an open source app\n Learn how to register both existing and new open source apps for distribution.\nGuide\n Limited distribution accounts are now available\n Learn how students, teachers, and hobbyists can share apps with up to 20 devices without a government-issued ID or registration fee.\nBlog\n Android developer verification: Building a safer ecosystem together\n An update on developer verification, including regional enforcement details starting September 30, 2026, for select stores, and new APIs to automate workflows.\nBlog\n Rolling out to all developers on Play and Android consoles\n Over the next few weeks, we're opening the verification process to everyone through Android Developer Console and the Play Console.\nBlog\n Balancing openness and choice with safety\n Preview our advanced flow to ensure power users can sideload apps from unverified developers.\nYouTube\n Preview how users can sideload your apps\n Watch a quick explainer on how the new advanced flow works.\nhref=\"https://developer.android.com/developer-verification/guides/open-source-app-registration\"\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8263a2d0-7a74-4d55-80cb-40597ee31eb7","uuid":"2c8d1818-661b-4fae-960c-53f6c3a23461","timestamp":"2026-10-17T14:54:40.956Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" Play Console APIs ↗️\n the Android Developer's Blog\n Read the latest\n Explore the authors →\n Explore 