{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pp7idoTLCRmW76VAbf8LRn","type":"tool_result","content":"571 oss.txt\n Play Programs ↗️\n Games Dev Center\n Overview\n Play Asset Delivery\n Play Games Services\n Play Games on PC\n Level Up guidelines\n All Play guides ⤵️\n Libraries\n Play Feature Delivery\n Play In-app Updates\n Play In-app Reviews\n Play Install Referrer\n Google Play services ↗️\n Google Play SDK index ↗️\n All Play libraries ⤵️\n Tools & resources\n Android App Bundles\n Brand & marketing\n Play Console APIs ↗️\n the Android Developer's Blog\n Read the latest\n Explore the authors →\n Explore categories\n Product News\n Community\n How-tos\n Case Studies\n Events & Programs\n Documentation\n Android Developers\n Essentials\n Android developer verification\n Guides\n Register your app on open source platforms\n Stay organized with collections\n Save and categorize content based on your preferences.\nThis guide explains how to register your apps on open source platforms. The\nprocess is similar to \ndistributing your app\n through other stores. While you\ndon't have to register your app in order to continue distributing them on open\nsource platforms, doing so will let your users continue with the same install\nexperience they have today.\nBefore you begin, set up an \nAndroid Developer Console\n account or \nGoogle\nPlay Console\n account. If you don't have an account, sign up by following the\ndeveloper verification guide\n.\nNote:\n If you are distributing the app through a store that integrates with the\nAndroid Developer Console API\n, the store can handle the package name and\nkey registration process on your behalf. You still need a verified Android\nDeveloper Console account or Play Console account to link the app to your\nidentity.\nChoose how users install your app\nDepending on whether you verify and register, users can install your app in one\nof two ways:\nNo changes for your users.\n Register your apps to your verified identity\nso users can install it just like they always have.\nAdvanced flow setup.\n If you prefer not to register your app, users can\nenable advanced flow on their device. This one-time setup allows them to\ninstall apps from unverified developers.\nRegister a new app\nComplete the following steps to register a new app.\nIn the \nAndroid Developer Console\n or the Android developer verification\ntab on \nGoogle Play Console\n, click \nRegister package name\n.\nEnter the package name of your new app, and click \nNext\n.\nClick \nAdd key\n, and enter the SHA-256 certificate fingerprint of your\nsigning key. See the \nHelp Center guide\n for instructions on extracting\nthe fingerprint. If the open source platform uses your signing key to\ndistribute the app, you don't need to complete any further steps.\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8263a2d0-7a74-4d55-80cb-40597ee31eb7","uuid":"71abf750-27a8-4518-acf1-75781bf6dfb6","timestamp":"2026-10-17T14:54:45.681Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"571 oss.txt\n Play Programs ↗️\n Games Dev Center\n Overview\n Play Asset Delivery\n Play Games Services\n Play Games on PC\n Level Up guidelines\n All Play guides ⤵️\n Libraries\n Play Feature Delivery\n Play In-app Updates\n Play In-app Reviews\n Play Install Referrer\n Google Play services ↗️\n Google Play SDK index ↗️\n All Play libraries ⤵️\n Tools & resources\n Android App Bundles\n Brand & marketing\n Play Console APIs ↗️\n the Android Developer's Blog\n Read the latest\n Explore the authors →\n Explore categories\n Product News\n Community\n How-tos\n Case Studies\n Events & Programs\n Documentation\n Android Developers\n Essentials\n Android developer verification\n Guides\n Register your app on open source platforms\n Stay organized with collections\n Save and categorize content based on your preferences.\nThis guide explains how to register your apps on open source platforms. The\nprocess is similar to \ndistributing your app\n through other stores. While you\ndon't have to register your app in order to continue distributing them on open\nsource platforms, doing so will let your users continue with the same install\nexperience they have today.\nBefore you begin, set up an \nAndroid Developer Console\n account or \nGoogle\nPlay Console\n account. If you don't have an account, sign up by following the\ndeveloper verification guide\n.\nNote:\n If you are distributing the app through a store that integrates with the\nAndroid Developer Console API\n, the store can handle the package name and\nkey registration process on your behalf. You still need a verified Android\nDeveloper Console account or Play Console account to link the app to your\nidentity.\nChoose how users install your app\nDepending on whether you verify and register, users can install your app in one\nof two ways:\nNo changes for your users.\n Register your apps to your verified identity\nso users can install it just like they always have.\nAdvanced flow setup.\n If you prefer not to register your app, users can\nenable advanced flow on their device. This one-time setup allows them to\ninstall apps from unverified developers.\nRegister a new app\nComplete the following steps to register a new app.\nIn the \nAndroid Developer Console\n or the Android developer verification\ntab on \nGoogle Play Console\n, click \nRegister package name\n.\nEnter the package name of your new app, and click \nNext\n.\nClick \nAdd key\n, and enter the SHA-256 certificate fingerprint of your\nsigning key. See the \nHelp Center guide\n for instructions on extracting\nthe fingerprint. If the open source platform uses your signing key to\ndistribute the app, you don't need to complete any further steps.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pp7idoTLCRmW76VAbf8LRn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config"