atasafety https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/10787469\ngrep -n -iE \"encrypted in transit|ephemeral|collected|shared|service provider\" datasafety.txt | head -12\nget ugc https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/9876937\ngrep -n -iE \"in-app|report|block|terms of use\" ugc.txt | head -10\ncurl -sSL -m 30 https://developer.apple.com/tutorials/data/documentation/security/complying-with-encryption-export-regulations.json -o exp.json; python3 -I -c \"\nimport json,re;s=open('/tmp/dl/exp.json').read()\nfor k in ['ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption','exempt','HTTPS']:\n  for m in list(re.finditer(k,s))[:2]: print(s[max(0,m.start()-150):m.start()+200].replace('\\\\\\\\n',' '));print('--')\""}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RMWVMKA4AUat6vxmvEeSP2","type":"tool_result","content":"1118 datasafety.txt\n64:All developers must declare how they collect and handle user data for the apps they publish on Google Play, and provide details about how they protect this data through security practices like encryption. This includes data collected and handled through any third-party libraries or SDKs used in their apps. You may want to refer to your SDK providers’ published Data safety information for details. Check \n85:Even developers with apps that do not collect any user data must complete this form and provide a link to their privacy policy. In this case, the completed form and privacy policy can indicate that no user data is collected or shared.\n123: It also includes user data collected from a webview which has been opened from your app, if your app is in control of the code/behavior delivered through that webview.\n125:Ephemeral processing: \n126:User data transmitted off device that is processed ephemerally needs to be included in your form response, but if it meets the standard below, it will \n129:Processing data \"ephemerally\" means accessing and using it while the data is only stored in memory and retained for no longer than necessary to service the specific request in real-time.\n130:For example, a weather app that transmits user location off the device to fetch the current weather at the user's location but only uses location data in memory and does not store that data once the request has been fulfilled, can treat its transient use of location as ephemeral. However, using data to build advertising profiles or other user profiles cannot be treated as ephemeral and must be declared as collection or sharing for the relevant purposes.\n132:User data collected pseudonymously must be disclosed. For example, data that can reasonably be re-associated with a user must be disclosed.\n134:The following use cases do not need to be disclosed as collected:\n145:\"Sharing\" refers to transferring user data collected from your app to a third party. Thi\n151:For example, if you transfer user data collected from your app from your server to a third-party server.\n155:Transferring data collected from your app off a user’s device directly to a third party via libraries and/or SDKs included in your app.\n222 ugc.txt\n61:Apps with user-generated content must have robust moderation to ensure a safe environment. You must provide clear terms of use, an in-app system for reporting objectionable content, and a function for users to block others. Incidental sexual content must be filtered by default and restricted from minors. Please review the full policy to ensure compliance.\n65:Requires users accept the app's terms of use and/or user policy before users can create or upload UGC;\n66:Defines objectionable content and behaviors (in a way that complies with Google Play Developer Program Policies), and prohibits them in the app’s terms of use or user policies;\n67:Conducts UGC moderation, as is reasonable and consistent with the type of UGC hosted by the app. This includes providing an in-app system for reporting and blocking objectionable UGC and users, and taking action against UGC or users where appropriate. Different UGC experiences may require different moderation efforts. For example:\n68:Apps featuring UGC that identify a specified set of users through means such as user verification or offline registration (for example, apps exclusively used within a specific school or company, etc.) must provide in-app functionality to report content and users.\n69:UGC features that enable 1:1 user interaction with specific users (for example, direct messaging, tagging, mentioning, etc.) must provide an in-app functionality for blocking users.\n70:Apps that provide access to publicly accessible UGC, such as social networking apps and blogger apps, must implement in-app functionality to report users and content, and to block users.\n71:In the case of augmented reality (AR) apps, UGC moderation (including the in-app reporting system) must account for both objectionable AR UGC (for example, a sexually explicit AR image) and sensitive AR anchoring location (for example, AR content anchored to a restricted area, such as a military base, or a private property where AR anchoring may cause issues for the property owner).\n72:Provides safeguards to prevent in-app monetization from encouraging objectionable user behavior.\n96:Require users to accept your app's terms of use before they create or upload UGC.\nontent\":[{\"text\":\"Add the \",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"identifier\":\"doc:\\/\\/com.apple.documentation\\/documentation\\/BundleResources\\/Information-Property-List\\/ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption\",\"isActive\":true,\"type\":\"reference\"},{\"text\":\" key to your app’s information property list with a Boolean value that indicates whether your app uses encryption. Set the v\n--\nchor\":\"Encryption-Export-Compliance-Keys\",\"identifiers\":[\"doc:\\/\\/com.apple.documentation\\/documentation\\/BundleResources\\/Information-Property-List\\/ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption\",\"doc:\\/\\/com.apple.documentation\\/documentation\\/BundleResources\\/Information-Property-List\\/ITSEncryptionExportComplianceCode\"],\"title\":\"Encryption Export Compliance Ke\n--\n\"},{\"text\":\" if your app—including any third-party libraries it links against—doesn’t use encryption, or if it only uses forms of encryption that are exempt from export compliance documentation requirements. Otherwise, set it to \",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"code\":\"YES\",\"type\":\"codeVoice\"},{\"text\":\".\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"type\":\"paragraph\"},{\"inlineContent\":[{\"id\n--\ntype\":\"text\"},{\"identifier\":\"doc:\\/\\/com.apple.documentation\\/documentation\\/Foundation\\/URLSession\",\"isActive\":true,\"type\":\"reference\"},{\"text\":\"—is exempt from export documentation upload requirements, whereas the use of proprietary encryption is not. To determine whether your use of encryption is considered exempt, see \",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"identif\n--\nype\":\"paragraph\"},{\"inlineContent\":[{\"text\":\"Typically, the use of encryption that’s built into the operating system—for example, when your app makes HTTPS connections using \",\"type\":\"text\"},{\"identifier\":\"doc:\\/\\/com.apple.documentation\\/documentation\\/Foundation\\/URLSession\",\"isActive\":true,\"type\":\"reference\"},{\"text\":\"—is exempt from export docu\n--\nShell cwd was reset to /workspace","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8263a2d0-7a74-4d55-80cb-40597ee31eb7","uuid":"927e004e-de3e-499b-a845-e0d99335c633","timestamp":"2026-10-17T14:55:47.690Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1118 datasafety.txt\n64:All developers must declare how they collect and handle user data for the apps they publish on Google Play, and provide details about how they protect this data through security practices like encryption. This includes data collected and handled through any third-party libraries or SDKs used in their apps. You may want to refer to your SDK providers’ published Data safety information for details. Check \n85:Even developers with apps that do not collect any user data must complete this form and provide a link to their privacy policy. In this case, the completed form and privacy policy can indicate that no user data is collected or shared.\n123: It also includes user data collected from a webview which has been opened from your app, if your app is in control of the code/behavior delivered through that webview.\n125:Ephemeral processing: \n126:User data transmitted off device that is processed ephemerally needs to be included in your form response, but if it meets the standard below, it will \n129:Processing data \"ephemerally\" means accessing and using it while the data is only stored in memory and retained for no longer than necessary to service the specific request in real-time.\n130: