 (§7), phased\n  plan (§8), costs and accounts (§9), work split by repo (§10), open\n  questions (§11) and dated sources (§12). The style follows\n  `docs/reports/android-homescreen-widgets.md`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- Not verified (marked in the report): whether Capacitor 7 builds with\n  Xcode 26, WebAuthn in a Capacitor WKWebView with the `capacitor://`\n  scheme, Push API support in Android System WebView, whether F-Droid's\n  scanner accepts `node_modules/@capacitor/ios`, the EU DSA trader-status\n  details, and whether `app.solyto` is available as a Play package name and\n  as an Apple bundle ID.\n- Found in passing and outside the report's scope: the `versionCode`\n  formula collides once MINOR or PATCH goes above 99 (§7).\n  `allowBackup=\"true\"` may back up the WebView auth token (§3.1).\n- The canonical `../app` repo is not available here, so the check for\n  third-party contributors (relevant to AGPL on the App Store) only covers\n  this repo's history.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":19,"newStart":1,"newLines":79,"lines":[" # Implementation: play store and app store strategy"," "," id: jail","-developer:","-date:","+developer: @developer","+date: 2026-10-17"," ","-<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->","-"," ## Summary"," ","-<!-- What was implemented, task by task. Reference task IDs. -->","+This job produced one report, `docs/reports/play-store-and-app-store.md`.","+It lists the steps needed to publish solyto on Google Play and the Apple","+App Store. It is based on the repo as it is today and on official store,","+Capacitor, F-Droid and FSF pages fetched on 2026-10-17 (dated sources in","+§12). No code, Gradle, manifest, `patch/`, `frontend/`, `fdroid/`,","+`fastlane/`, CI or signing files were changed. No iOS project was created,","+and no release or store tooling was run."," ","+Main findings:","+- **Blockers for both stores:** there is no account deletion anywhere (no","+  API route, no UI; verified). UG